  "rules": {
    "oracle": "Essence Burn deals 5 damage to target black or green creature or planeswalker. If that permanent would die this turn, exile it instead.",
    "cr": [
      "115.1",
      "601.2c",
      "608.2b",
      "614.1a",
      "614.6",
      "700.4",
      "704.5g",
      "704.5i",
      "120.3c",
      "514.2"
    ],
    "actual": "Any black permanent (an enchantment, an artifact, a land) is a legal target, because the color split bound \"black\" to every card type. The second sentence is Unimplemented, so a creature or planeswalker the spell kills goes to its owner's graveyard instead of exile, and so does one that dies later that turn.",
    "expected": "The target must be a creature or planeswalker that is black or green (CR 115.1). If that permanent would die this turn, from this damage or anything else, it is exiled instead (CR 614.1a, 614.6; \"dies\" is CR 700.4: a creature or planeswalker put into a graveyard from the battlefield, which covers lethal damage, CR 704.5g, and 0 loyalty, CR 704.5i). The effect ends at the end of the turn (CR 514.2). If the target is illegal on resolution, the spell does nothing (CR 608.2b).",
    "diagnosis": "The target parser splits \"black or green creature or planeswalker\" as \"black\" | \"green creature\" | \"green planeswalker\", so the black branch gets type filter Any. The die-exile rider parser (try_parse_die_exile_rider) only accepts the subjects \"it\"/\"that creature\" and not \"that permanent\", so the sentence falls through to Unimplemented unparsed_replacement.",
    "suggested_fix": "In parser/oracle_target.rs, distribute a color disjunction over a following card-type disjunction: \"black or green creature or planeswalker\" should produce Or[Creature+Black, Planeswalker+Black, Creature+Green, Planeswalker+Green], never a bare Typed{Any, HasColor Black} branch. In parser/oracle_effect/mod.rs, let try_parse_die_exile_rider accept \"that permanent\" as its subject, producing the same AddTargetReplacement (event Moved, valid_card SelfRef, destination_zone Graveyard, execute ChangeZone Battlefield->Exile SelfRef, consume_on_apply, expiry EndOfTurn, target Any) that Agate Assault and Torch the Tower already get. Open PR #10032 does both.",
    "override_note": "The patch installs exactly the shape PR #10032's lowered snapshot gives the card: the four-way Creature/Planeswalker x Black/Green target, and the AddTargetReplacement rider byte-identical to Agate Assault's and Torch the Tower's. The rider is a replacement effect created on resolution (CR 614.1a) bound to the targeted permanent (valid_card SelfRef): when it would move from the battlefield to a graveyard this turn it is exiled instead. Creature lethal damage (CR 704.5g) and planeswalker zero loyalty (CR 704.5i) both route through the moved-replacement pipeline in 0.116.0, and the rider is pruned at cleanup (CR 514.2). The rest of PR #10032's runtime work keeps resolution-created replacements across face changes and copy effects (CR 707.2, 708, 710), which a plain creature or planeswalker never meets in play."
  },
